hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.12957144076010407,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":64.8,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.44411325298212445,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":26.0,"_gate_incr_roic":-0.07206250569676799,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":0.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.030984922068798264,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":23.0,"_gate_pool_share":-0.23032279621452556,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.03320811838525528,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":41.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.10504193585376354,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.01693804607075684,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":16.9,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06771067943737533,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":86.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.008264273576529257,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":39.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.005596960431829787,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":90.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.0991,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":66.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Hovnanian Enterprises, Inc., through its subsidiaries, designs, constructs, markets, and sells residential homes in the United States. It offers single-family detached homes, attached townhomes and condominiums, urban infill, and active lifestyle homes with amenities, such as clubhouses, swimming pools, tennis courts, tot lots, and open areas. The company markets and builds homes for first-time buyers, move-up buyers, luxury buyers, active lifestyle buyers, and empty nesters. It also provides mortgage loans and title services. Hovnanian Enterprises, Inc. was founded in 1959 and is based in Matawan, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ara K. Hovnanian | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 68 | Compensation: $6.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $88K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Hovnanian Enterprises, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $605M market cap on $3.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $166M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.67\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 9.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 92% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9185658949644173},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 59% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Director J. Larry Sorsby Sells 5,333 HOV Shares at $104.92 Each on November 2, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/director-j-larry-sorsby-sells-5333-hov-shares-at-10492-each-on-november-2-2026","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793857676.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Michael P. Wyatt Executes Tax-Withholding Sale of 3,893 HOV Shares on November 2, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/michael-p-wyatt-executes-tax-withholding-sale-of-3893-hov-